    "text": "<p>In the given figure, a mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> is attached to a horizontal spring which is fixed on one side to a rigid support. The spring constant of the spring is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The mass oscillates on a frictionless surface with time period <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> and amplitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;When the mass is in equilibrium position, as shown in the figure, another mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is gently fixed upon it. The new amplitude of oscillation will be:</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/34d25494-1f17-4bdb-b09a-c82419d6e17f-image.png\" style=\"width: 270px; height: 193px;\" /></p>",
